  "step_3": "The decision reason requires adjusting low-probability weights and computing a weighted sum to determine preference. While the individual acknowledges the low probabilities, they do not engage with probability weighting or any form of adjusted expectation. Instead, the individual uses a simple heuristic: when probabilities are similarly small, choose the one with the higher payoff. This aligns with the intuition behind the decision reason (attending to rare events), but the specific mechanism—explicit probability transformation and evaluation of weighted sums—is absent from the verbal report. The justification is outcome-focused rather than process-focused on probability transformation. Therefore, while there is surface-level consistency in attending to rare events, the actual cognitive procedure described does not match the formal rule of the decision reason.",
